   feature:{kicker:'Featured technology', title:'Exomind™', tagline:'Focused brain stimulation. No medication, no downtime.', img:'uploads/THERAPY_Exomind_crop.png',
     lead:'Exomind™ is a next-generation transcranial magnetic stimulation (TMS) system from BTL. It is non-invasive and drug-free, and sits alongside psychology at THERAPY™ as another way to support mood, focus and emotional resilience.',
     how:['TMS has been used in clinical settings for well over a decade. Earlier systems often meant long, frequent appointments that were hard to keep up with. Exomind™ uses BTL’s ExoTMS™ technology to make sessions shorter and simpler.',
          'A treatment head sits gently against the scalp and delivers focused magnetic pulses to the dorsolateral prefrontal cortex (DLPFC), the region of the brain involved in mood regulation, decision-making and emotional processing. Stimulating this area is designed to increase activity and connectivity in networks that can become under-active under chronic stress and low mood. You stay seated, awake and comfortable throughout.'],
     benefits:[{h:'Non-invasive',t:'No surgery, needles or anaesthetic.'},{h:'Drug-free',t:'Works through targeted stimulation rather than medication, so there are no medication side effects.'},{h:'Under 30 minutes',t:'Walk in, walk out, and return to your day straight away.'},{h:'Targeted',t:'Focused on the brain region most closely linked with mood and emotional regulation.'}],
     who:'Exomind™ may suit people experiencing low mood, anxious or obsessive thinking, brain fog, or compulsive eating and drinking patterns, particularly those who prefer a non-pharmaceutical option or have not found medication helpful. Suitability is always assessed first.',
     expect:[{h:'Consultation',t:'We talk through your symptoms, history and goals and confirm whether Exomind™ is appropriate for you.'},{h:'Your plan',t:'If it is, we build a personalised course. Number and frequency of sessions are tailored to you.'},{h:'Sessions',t:'Each one takes under 30 minutes. Many people describe feeling calm and clear afterwards.'},{h:'Progress',t:'Results vary between people. Changes are often noticed over a series of sessions, and we review as you go.'}],
     faqs:[{q:'Does it replace therapy or medication?',a:'No. Exomind™ is part of an integrative approach and can complement psychology and existing care. Never stop or change prescribed medication without speaking to your doctor.'},{q:'Does it hurt?',a:'Most people feel a light tapping sensation on the scalp and hear a clicking sound. There is no anaesthetic and no recovery time.'},{q:'How many sessions will I need?',a:'It depends on your needs and goals. We recommend a course rather than a single session and tailor it after your consultation.'},{q:'Can I combine it with other services?',a:'Yes. Many clients pair Exomind™ with psychology, the NeuroSuite or our Nervous System Reset program.'},{q:'How do I know if hormones are affecting my mood?',a:'Anxiety, irritability, poor concentration, mood swings and disrupted sleep can all point to hormonal change. A blood panel shows whether hormones such as oestrogen, testosterone, cortisol or thyroid hormones are playing a part.'},{q:'How often should bloodwork be repeated?',a:'We start with a baseline panel and recommend a retest interval based on your results, goals and plan.'},{q:'Do I need a specific diagnosis or medication to be eligible?',a:'No. Exomind™ and our testing are open to anyone wanting clearer thinking, steadier mood and better resilience under stress, after a suitability consultation.'}],
     context:{title:'Mental health is biological too', lead:'Mood, focus and resilience are shaped by more than thoughts and circumstances. Hormones, cortisol rhythm, nutrients, inflammation and metabolism all influence how your brain feels and functions. Bloodwork and a 4-point saliva cortisol test show us what is really going on. That is why Exomind™ sits inside a wider assessment rather than on its own.',
       blocks:[{h:'Why we test your blood and saliva',t:'Comprehensive bloodwork, together with a 4-point saliva cortisol test, can reveal drivers of low mood, anxiety and brain fog that are easy to miss. These results help us build a plan for both mind and body, which may include nutrition, supplementation, IV therapy, psychology or Exomind™.',list:['Hormones — oestrogen, progesterone, testosterone and thyroid','4-point saliva cortisol — your stress-hormone rhythm from waking to bedtime','Nutrients — vitamin B12, vitamin D, magnesium and iron','Inflammation and oxidative stress markers','Metabolic and adrenal function']},
               {h:'Menopause, hormones and mood',t:'Perimenopause and menopause can bring anxiety, poor sleep, irritability and low mood, driven by significant hormonal change. These symptoms are not simply part of getting older. They are signals worth understanding, and with the right testing and support you can feel like yourself again.'},
               {h:'Mental health on GLP-1 medication',t:'GLP-1 medications can be very effective for weight management, but some people notice muscle loss, low energy or changes in mood along the way. If you are on a GLP-1 prescribed by your doctor, we can support you alongside them with metabolic testing, strength and muscle-preserving programs, nutrition and mental wellbeing care, so weight loss does not come at the cost of clarity or vitality.'},{h:'Why the mind comes first',t:'Anxiety, low motivation, broken sleep and brain fog make it harder to keep up healthy routines, make clear decisions and get the most from any treatment. Supporting your mental wellbeing first makes everything else work better.'}]},
     note:'Exomind™ is a wellness technology and is not a substitute for medical or psychiatric diagnosis or treatment. If you are in crisis, call Lifeline on 13 11 14 or 000 in an emergency.', href:BOOK, cta:'Book an Exomind™ consultation'},
